registry.coffee public dataset: data licence

The public dataset of coffee-data-tracker (registry.coffee) is made available under the Community Data License
Agreement - Permissive, Version 2.0 (CDLA-Permissive-2.0), whose full text follows below. It covers:

  - the public tables: public_coffee, public_roaster, public_price_event and public_market_weekly, as defined by
    contracts/public-catalog.odcs.yaml;
  - their exports: the Parquet files and manifest.json written by `coffeedata export-public`, including the
    public Hugging Face dataset jtouley/us-coffee-market;
  - the site's catalog JSON (https://registry.coffee/catalog/catalog.json);
  - the marketplace shares of those tables: the Snowflake share of COFFEE_DATA.SHARE and, when set up, the
    Databricks share.

The code in this repository is under the MIT License (LICENSE), not this one.

Attribution
  - Roaster discovery uses Overture Maps Places, (c) Overture Maps Foundation, licensed under CDLA-Permissive-2.0.
    Source datasets carry their own attribution, listed in the Overture release notes.
  - Roasters known only from OpenStreetMap are excluded from the public tables, so OpenStreetMap's ODbL
    share-alike terms don't apply to them.
  - Coffee names and prices are facts published by each roaster on its own storefront; every coffee links back to
    it through source_url. Product descriptions and images are not included.
  See docs/ATTRIBUTION.md.

